{
  "_about": [
    "Per-source reuse policy for the News feed (save-trends.mjs). The feed always shows title + link to the source.",
    "image: the article og:image, shown as a link-preview thumbnail next to the headline. Publishers emit og:image so that",
    "other surfaces (social, chat, aggregators) render exactly this preview; we show it at card size and link out. Default true.",
    "Set image:false on a source that objects (robots/ToS says no previews, or hotlinks are blocked) and note why in evidence.",
    "summary: the article description (og:description, <=280 chars) — that is article text, so it stays off until permission",
    "is recorded in evidence (terms-of-service URL / license / written agreement) with the date in checked.",
    "Unknown sources fall back to _default. Video thumbnails come from the YouTube API and are not governed here."
  ],
  "_default": {
    "image": true,
    "summary": false
  },
